        "username": "aireview",
        "status": "Contact Oleg Drokin (green@whamcloud.com) with any questions on this account"
      },
      "date": "2026-11-26 13:54:20.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\n(3 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nThe kernel-side fix looks correct: every put and nest start is now checked, the partial entry is cancelled, and the dump resumes at the right index on both old and new kernels. The two points that need a refresh are the regression test, which probably never spans more than one skb (see inline), and the missing Fixes: tag. A separate, pre-existing issue: lnet_ping_cmd(), the `lnetctl discover` path in the same file, still calls nla_nest_start() and nla_put_*() without checking them on a fixed NLMSG_GOODSIZE reply. With enough discover targets it can hit the same NULL nla_nest_end() write. That probably deserves its own ticket and patch.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 2
    }
