        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Serguei Smirnov",
          "email": "ssmirnov@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-26 00:49:36.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21332 lnet: rewind the ping dump when an entry does not fit",
        "message": "LU-21332 lnet: rewind the ping dump when an entry does not fit\n\n\"lnetctl ping\" with a few hundred targets oopsed the node with a NULL\nwrite in lnet_ping_show_dump(), called from netlink_dump().\n\nWhen the skb filled, nla_nest_start() returned NULL and nla_nest_end()\nwrote through it.  Failure of genlmsg_put() also left lgpl_index stale\nand leaked the peer's list.  If the dump resumed from the old index,\nit would ping targets again.  At index 0 it resent the key table and\nre-initialised lgpl_failed under a stale lgpl_failed_count.  The\nfailed-ping section restarted from entry 0 as well.\nlnet_genl_parse_list() also ignored failed puts, so a key table added\nto a partly filled skb could go out incomplete.\n\nCheck all attribute insertions and nest allocations.  On a full skb,\ndrop the partial entry, free the peer list and rewind one entry, then\nreturn msg->len, or -EMSGSIZE when the entry does not fit by itself.\nSend the key tables and headers only once, initialise lgpl_failed in\nlnet_ping_show_start() and give the failed list its own index.\nMake lnet_genl_parse_list() return -EMSGSIZE for a full skb so that\nthe failed-ping key table can be retried in the next dump round.\n\nAlso return -ENOMEM, not the ping error, when a failed-ping entry\ncannot be allocated, free the peer list on that path and increment\nlgpl_failed_count only after successful allocation.\n\nAdd sanity-lnet test_247, which pings enough targets in one command\nto exercise dump continuation and verifies the total reply count.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTLC-bug-id: TLU-341\nSigned-off-by: Minh Diep <mdiep@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: Ib3cd58d3a2216fdcee4c4730fe82550963236fb9\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
